WEBVTT

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.030
<i>Six months have passed since the new students began their school lives in April.</i>

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.750
<i>All the trees on campus have changed color, and we are in the midst of autumn.</i>

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.810
<i>One of Yumegaoka High School's most important days is fast approaching. {## parallel subject change, dodges 'we are' again}</i>

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.390
Everything is so high level! {## 'high-level' if you must, as a single adjective}

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.030
Whoa!

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:31.920
Sorry!

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.070
Be careful.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:33.930
Okay!

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.430
Katori-sensei!

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.680
Towano-sensei. {## if he's gonna show up this much can they give the poor man some fucking eyes?}

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.770
Sure is freezing.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.140
The temperature drops fast when the sun sets. {## 'sun is setting' / 'fast as' reads like 'as fast as'}

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.720
Days like this make me want to gulp down a hot one.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.390
Uh, it's days like <i>this</i> that you especially shouldn't.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.150
You got me there.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.440
Tomorrow's the big day! Don't lose steam now! {## alt. 'Keep at it!' / 'don't lose motivation' isn't a very... good phrase of encouragement; too weak, among other things}

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.830
<i>The only day all year when students are permitted to stay at school overnight.</i>

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.750
<i>Everyone is elated by the buzz of excitement leading up to the school festival. {## at another time I might have picked a fight over 'cultural' since there are two different terms being used}</i>

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.720
<i>Yes, it is an extraordinary night in an ordinary place.</i>

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.680
<i>The night before the Yumegaoka High School Festival.</i>

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:24.410
<i>From the thick of the unusual atmosphere permeating the school, </i>he<i> might appear once again. {## structure for emphasis / alt. have 'unordinary' if you must, but it's weird. 'atypical', 'unusual'}</i>

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.440
<i>Don't you dare...</i>

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>even think of messing with my precious students, Peter.</i>

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:40.190
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:40.190
hanashitakatta koto takusan atta no ni

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.530
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.530
kao miru to wasurechau

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:54.140
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:54.140
houkago mukae ni kitekureru no ga ureshikute

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.390
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.390
doushite kimi ja nakucha dame na no kana

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:15.140
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:15.140
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.530
The days have begun to get shorter now

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.530
hi ga mijikaku nattekita ne

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:30.660
Why must they cut off my time with you?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:30.660
mou chotto issho ni itai no ni

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.270
Tomorrow and the day after, and every day forevermore

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.270
ashita mo asatte mo sono saki mo zutto

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:41.420
I want to keep walking home together like this

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:41.420
kouyatte kimi to kaeritai

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:46.870
No matter what the weather was, no matter how my day went

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:46.870
donna tenki demo donna kibun demo

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:54.640
The moment you raise your hand to wave goodbye

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:54.640
mata ne to kimi ga te wo furu toki

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:02.620
I feel like it has been a wonderful day

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:02.620
ii hi datta to omoeru kara

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.330
About the Eternal
School Festival

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.000
Hey, Ane-san...

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.770
What exactly are you putting together there?

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.800
Come on, isn't it obvious?

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.790
They're pitcher plants.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.620
And this here's a rafflesia.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.140
Yeah. It's disgusting.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.730
Please, are you trying to make me blush with that wonderful compliment?

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.190
My class is opening a Jungle Café outside on the grounds.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.720
Okay, but that doesn't explain the disturbing decorations...

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.300
You ain't seen nothing yet. {## 'You ain't seen nothin' yet.'}

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:41.170
I'm going to make all of these, too!

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.600
They're all disgusting! {## it's a repeat, may as well}

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.290
You flatter me!

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.740
I'm not trying to.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.640
All right, take these. {## since immediately afterwards they're referred to as 'they'}

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.150
They're materials for the rafflesia. 
Bring it back once you finish making it.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.590
Why should I have to help a different class?

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:59.420
It looks like I'm not even allowed to question that.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.270
Thanks in advance!

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.390
Ane-chan-senpai...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.070
Good evening...

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.050
Tekochin!

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.220
What happened to you?

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.020
Heya!

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.100
Would you like a drink to relieve your fatigue?

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:21.280
You're the one who looks about to collapse...

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.050
We're selling drinks class-to-class.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.400
Selling drinks?

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:26.910
Yes!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.120
Our class is making mosaic art out of paper drink boxes. {they're not all juice}

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.340
But the thing is, we don't have nearly enough.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.810
Sounds rough.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.500
They're fifty yen each.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.820
All right, guess I'll have one.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.460
Please, no need to restrain yourself! {## alt. 'hold back' / orig. sounds like 'as many as you like [for 50en]}

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.030
One is more than enough!

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.380
What kinds do you ha—

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:44.380
Here!

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.090
What?! I don't get to choose?

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:49.560
I'm equipped with an automatic selection function.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.870
Ick, bitter melon?! {## kids these days}

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.020
We need a lot of that color.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.730
Would anyone else like one?

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.230
I recommend the bitter melon juice.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.780
Uh, no thanks. {## don't appreciate its glory}

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.190
Bitter melon is kinda...

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.150
What else do you have?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:10.750
Let's see... Strawberry milk, yogurt, lemon juice, and café au lait. {## oh no you don't, not even Cambridge has 'yoghurt' as primary / 'lemon juice'?!}

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.530
But you're not allowed to pick!

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.800
Uh, I'd be okay with café au lait, but...  {## '[but not with bitter melon]'}

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.280
I only want strawberry milk... {## it's not an expression of preference but rather that they explicitly will only buy if they get those}

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.920
No being picky!

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.420
I'll... let them be picky. {## very strange to pause between 'let' and 'them', for reasons}

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.880
We have no other option.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.930
Hey, then let me switch to strawberry milk!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:27.990
Denied. {## 'Refused', 'Error'}

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:32.860
Now, now, Ninomiya. It's bad manners to change your mind after making a decision. {## similarly duplicative. two commas is -correct-: 'now, now' uses the comma, and the second is vocative and stop leaving it out}

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.560
Homeroom, when'd you get here? {## this is a bit derogatory, which is fine if it's also that way in the Japanese, I'm not sure / there isn't a good way around it that I can see, either ('Sensei')}{most people also don't say mato-chan-sensei}

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.330
Towano-sensei.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.960
Oh, you two are from Katori-sensei's class.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:39.560
Yes. {## you may disagree, but this seems the more natural response in English, cool literalness aside}

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.940
Looks like you still have a ton left.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:47.450
All right! I'll buy everything you've got for my class!

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.780
Even the bitter melon juice?

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.040
Of course!

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.220
Guys, you all love bitter melon, right? {## especially with the next line}

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.750
No...

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.330
Don't worry! You'll like it once you try it!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.780
Nice empty promise...

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:02.080
Ninomiya! I'll cover yours too!

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.710
Thanks, I guess.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.960
There we go.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.970
Gather round, class! This is a gift from your 
generous teacher! Drink as much as you want! {## 'benevolent' 'magnanimous'}

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.990
This is to help Katori-sensei's class get enough drink boxes.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.010
Don't leave a single one undrunk. {## sounds like 'drink like half of every one'}

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:19.440
After you finish each box, rinse it out 
with water and put it in this case.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.400
Does that sound right?

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:26.610
Gratitude! Gratitude!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.430
Don't be shy.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.070
It's almost entirely bitter melon.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:35.380
Towano-sensei is such a good teacher!

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:37.600
He really cares for his students.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:37.110
Dibs on the strawberry milk.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:39.100
You'll be drinking too, right Sensei?

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.270
Of course he will.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:43.320
Hold up, there! If I have one, then it's not a gift anymore.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.470
No excuses.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.260
You have to drink too! {## is that SAKURA AYANE}

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.180
You need to be health-conscious at your age.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.550
Stop resisting!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.550
All right, all right! I'll take the plunge and drink first. {## ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT ALRIGHT}

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:57.500
What a mysterious feeling. {## 'feels mysterious' kind of like 'feels suspicious', diff from 'mysterious feeling' somewhat}

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.390
Mysterious?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:02.650
Everyone is usually only together at school during the day,

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:09.650
but despite it being night now, we're all talking and laughing like always.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:14.910
It's like we've unknowingly wandered into a different world. {## note: chigau, and not i like the rest}

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.760
It feels strange. {## 'feels strange' and 'strange feeling' are close enough, though}

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.540
I think so too.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.370
Oops!

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.730
Pikari, we need to sell more drinks!

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:23.960
Right!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.370
Ane-chan-senpai, thanks for helping!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.410
Keep it up!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:28.290
We will!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.340
Is Towano-sensei here?

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.060
Sure is.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:44.040
So they foisted a bitter melon one 
on you. The taste must be incredible. {## 'taste incredible' is too... good}

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:49.370
Sure is. Well, for my darling underclassmen's sakes.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.610
Sorry.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.720
Katori-sensei! Thank you for doing the rounds. {## give the man some EYES}

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.980
Are all of the students staying overnight accounted for?

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:03.080
Yeah. I checked the ones outside too, so we're all clear.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.210
Everyone, you looking forward to tomorrow?

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.170
Yeah!

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:14.770
I'll check on all the other classes later too, so rest assured.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:16.640
Then I'll leave it to you.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:21.950
Katori-sensei.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:22.560
Yes?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.060
Where are you headed to next?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.440
I'm going outside.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:32.710
Uh... right! I forgot I had to check on the firewood for the bonfire! {## Uh...oh! reads as 'uh-oh', because it reads as one sentence, because these are actually two (three) sentences / I know he says 'campfire' but it's really a bonfire in this case}

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.340
May I tag along with you?

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.980
Huh? Yeah, sure.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.490
I'll be right out.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.040
Gross.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.000
Okay, it looks good to go.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.880
You'd better do your job and make a nice, big blaze on the final day.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:56.430
I like this spot.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.410
You can look out at every single class.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:02.190
Everyone's working hard.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:04.990
This atmosphere sure brings back memories.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:11.200
Back then, I would wish for time to stop on nights like this. {## 'back then' and 'used to' bleh}

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:17.620
If morning never came, I'd be able to enjoy the fun forever.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:25.430
I wonder if people feel scared about special times like these ending and having to return to the ordinary.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.750
Scared, huh.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.620
You might be right.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.260
Attention!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.250
We almost have enough empty boxes!

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:43.270
Gathering squad, let's keep it up for the final stretch!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.720
Move out!

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.030
Roger!

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.460
Ooh, that's a nice echo.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.170
It's so quiet.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:25.330
It's so late at night, but there are lights here and there all throughout the school. {## looking out, as it were}

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.350
Everyone's working hard.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.540
<i>It's quiet.</i>

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.270
The bustle of the classroom feels so distant now.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:48.160
It's like we've been sent somewhere far away.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.090
I don't dislike this atmosphere. {## 'atmosphere' the much more common word, ambience also carrying connotations of music or any other special effect}

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.130
Come on, we need to sell these like hotcakes!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.120
Right!

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.600
What, are you slacking?

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:23.160
What, are you hitting on me?

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:26.660
Everyone sure is working hard.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:36.630
This almost feels like a totally different space than the bustle over there.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.840
I don't dislike this feeling.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:47.010
I guess I wasn't the only one who thought so.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.050
I was just thinking the same thing.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.960
This must be some kind of fate.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.650
Come skip out on work with me for a while.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:05.870
<i>Is he asking me to take his hand?</i>

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:09.910
No, thank you. I need to be getting back to class.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:14.410
<i>Shoot, I stood up too fast! {and got dizzy. it's different from numb legs}{## happens to me all the time. vision blacks out for like ten seconds}</i>

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.050
<i>What's going on? {## HETERO PHYSICS}</i>

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.790
<i>It's like I'm flying!</i>

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.790
You okay?

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:54.670
Yeah. Thanks.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:55.750
You're very welcome.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.010
Now then, let's go.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.960
<i>Does he mean skipping work? {## 'mean to' reads as 'intend to' and is kind of formal}</i>

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.970
<i>Well, I guess I can spare some time.</i>

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.430
<i>He did save me just now, after all. {## the, uh, fifth? time, fuckin ichiou}</i>

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.680
Hey, what's your name? {## this sentence has been -ruined- for me utterly}

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.680
Ninomiya Ai.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.140
What about you? {## ANTA}

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:16.900
My name?

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.280
What's your deal?

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.390
Let's see...

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:28.780
You can call me Peter.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:39.790
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.250
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.720
<i></i>Naze<i>? How did this happen? {## FINALLY, GOOD WORK}</i>

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.550
<i>It's almost like...</i>

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.220
<i>Almost exactly like...</i>

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.690
<i>We're going on a date!</i>

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:02.150
<i>Calm down, calm down! Just think about it logically.</i>

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:06.750
Hey.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:11.450
However you slice it, there's no way that "Peter" is your real name.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.040
You got me. You could call it a lovable nickname.

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:20.500
So you won't tell me your actual name, even after I told you mine. {## orig. 'even after I told me your actual name'}

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:25.070
The person I am right now doesn't have a name yet. {## this is definitely some fuckery / 'the new me'?}

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.840
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:29.550
Are you mad? {## umadbro?}

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:34.010
I'll teach you a magic spell to feel better.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:34.740
Huh?

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.270
Blue Stripes.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.970
"Blue Stripes"? What's that?

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.160
You s-saw my panties?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:53.660
I did.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.500
No way! {## any variant of 'wait' seems like she's talking about the stairs that are about to appear}{she is}

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:07.210
<i>Okay... So I went to buy strawberry milk to wash out the bitter melon flavor.</i>

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:11.930
<i>Then I ran into this strange boy named Peter...</i>

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:14.930
<i>He asked me to skip out on work with him...</i>

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.230
<i>Just what in the world is going on?</i>

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:21.920
<i>Peter...</i>

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:24.650
What did you say?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.080
Ai still hasn't come back. {## no honorifics?! how rude}

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.350
You haven't seen her, Katori-sensei?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:30.070
No.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.380
She said she went to buy a drink.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:41.250
<i>I have the sensation we've been going in circles around the same places.</i>

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:43.710
<i>Light.</i>

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.040
<i>Dark.</i>

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.300
<i>Light.</i>

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.300
<i>Dark.</i>

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:55.480
<i>Little enclosed gardens of light shine here and there through the dark of night. {## darkness cannot be illuminated by definition: things are illuminated by the removal of darkness}</i>

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:58.520
<i>Could this be anything but another world? {## 'different world' seems somehow awkward. 'parallel', but kind of SF-ey.}</i>

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.190
Ai?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:07.150
I just slipped into a way of thinking very similar to one of my younger club members.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:14.740
<i>But it really is like I've wandered into another world, despite being in the same school as always.</i>

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:20.130
<i>Even if only for tonight,</i>

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:25.210
<i>the school may have transformed into a special place. {## avoid 'this' for the next lines}</i>

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.380
I wish it never had to end.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.820
You don't want it to ever end?

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:42.460
Yeah. I wish the school festival never had to start.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:47.280
I wish this fun, dreamlike time would last forever. {## eba like all the rest}

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.770
Hey, don't suddenly stop like that.

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:54.820
Ai.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:00.970
Do you truly want that? {## and now i'm dodging 'wish' because of the above}

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:10.460
Do you truly wish for this never to end?

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:17.220
W-Well, I guess. Still...

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:20.100
All fun things come to an end.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:23.610
That's why they're good.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:27.570
That's exactly why these times feel so dazzling.

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:28.400
Right?

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:27.910
Found you.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.580
Hey, what a surprise. If it isn't Mato-chan.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:32.290
Huh?

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.630
What do you plan on doing with her, Peter?

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.890
If she so desires, I was thinking of taking her with me. {## just gonna like avoid 'wish' forever}

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:48.560
How long do you plan on continuing to do this?

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.360
Who can say? But you can relax.

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:55.280
I only take those who want to go. {## for being more natural, and also allows it to be reflected in the later line}

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.330
You should already know that, Mato-chan.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.280
Bye, Ai.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:03.910
Peter...

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.050
Mato-chan-sensei, are you friends with Peter?

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.770
Yeah, you two were talking about those weird things and all that.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:22.390
Like "wanting to go" and "taking them". {## 'willingly wish' doesn't show up here, e.g.}

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.700
We've got a lot now!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.640
We're almost done with collection.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.810
Go help the building squad if you're finished.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:35.110
Roger!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.870
They're safe for now. {## 'so far'?}

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:38.610
Huh?

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:39.950
What?!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.550
Oh, Towano-sensei.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.160
Ninomiya! I've been looking for you.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.910
Um, I...

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:52.540
She was a little tired. I found her sleeping in the club room. Right?

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:56.490
Uh, yeah, right! I'm sorry.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.550
Geez, don't scare me like that.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:02.510
More importantly, have you noticed anything strange about the students?

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:06.530
No, I've checked on everyone, and they're all fine.

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:14.060
Um, could you tell me more about Peter?

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:20.510
What's his real name? Is he a third-year?

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.550
Don't get involved with him.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:31.040
He only appears at special times, like the nights before festivals. And then... {## generic}

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.420
He finds those who want those times to never end,

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:38.310
or children who don't want to become grown-ups, and takes them away. {## oh, it's motherfucking Peter -Pan-, OK, I get it}

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.590
He's a mischevious fairy.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.140
A fairy?

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:49.000
Oh please, there's no way!

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:53.850
Think about it. Remember the area above the stairs?

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:58.100
The landing with the vending machines is the top floor.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.780
The place he turned and left through

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.580
is a dead end.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:13.280
To be honest, I'm a bit more attuned to these things than the average person.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:19.350
Back when I was still a student at this school, I met him too.

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:35.390
He reached out his hand, not a single year younger or the slightest bit different from just earlier. {## this sounds like he was no older back then than now, which is the opposite of what's expected / I think the Japanese is just phrased weirdly}

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.610
I was invited as well.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:41.580
By Peter. {## Ane's hair is really nice this episode. fancy}

